@startuml
' MPSCRING-DOC-SDD, figure 4-2: where the library is built, delivered and linked (MPSCRING-IF-010, IF-011, CI-DEBS)
title MPSCring 1.0.10: delivery and linkage
skinparam shadowing false
node "build root (kyr-build 3.1.1)" as BR {
  artifact "libmpscring_1.0.10_amd64.deb\n/usr/local/lib/libmpscring.so.1.0.10\nsoname libmpscring.so.1" as RT
  artifact "libmpscring-dev_1.0.10_amd64.deb\n/usr/local/include/mpscring.h\n/usr/local/lib/libmpscring.a\nlibmpscring.so -> .so.1" as DEV
}
node "the platform's release train (kyr 0.40.0)" as TRAIN {
  artifact "deps.txt pins\nlibmpscring 1.0.8 sha256 6b2f27ee..." as PIN
}
node "the box" as BOX {
  component "kyr-server-* (kyr_server 3.14.0)\nlinks kyr_core, kyr_drive, kyr_estate,\nkyr_rms statically;\nlibmpscring.so.1 at run time" as SRV
}
DEV ..> RT : Depends: libmpscring (= 1.0.10)
RT --> PIN : published with the release\n(SHA256SUMS)
PIN --> SRV : installed by kyr-apply
note bottom of SRV
  exports: exactly the 8 functions of mpscring.h,
  each <name>@@MPSCRING_1 (utils/mpscring.map);
  a consumer built against another major fails at load
end note
@enduml
